  "body": "The specification of the pull method in [4.2.3](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#underlying-source-api) doesn't actually say how it's supposed to return new chunks. From [example 10.4](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#example-rs-pull) it seems that the way to return new chunks is to call controller.enqueue(), which is the same as a push source. But it should probably say so explicitly?\r\n\r\nOr, possibly this could be explained in the [mdn documentation](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ReadableStream/ReadableStream) if it doesn't belong in the spec. As it is, how to implement a push method is somewhat mysterious.\r\n\r\nSimilarly, to indicate that a stream is finished, it can call controller.close(), but this isn't actually said.",
